[?25l[0m[38;5;141m> [0mThe translation is correct — no divergence from the C was found, so [38;5;10msrc/lib.rs[0m is unchanged. The two real defects I found were in the verification harness, and one of them had made the whole suite meaningless.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m## What was wrong with the testing[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1m[38;5;10mcargo test[0m never built the [38;5;10mcdylib[0m.[22m With [38;5;10mcrate-type = ["cdylib"][0m and integration tests that don't link the crate, Cargo has no reason to emit [38;5;10mlibarity_lib.so[0m. My loader looked it up by path, found nothing in [38;5;10mtarget/debug/[0m, silently fell back to a [38;5;10mtarget/release/[0m copy built [3mbefore the tests existed[23m, and reported 48 green tests. I caught this by injecting 23 deliberate bugs into [38;5;10msrc/lib.rs[0m: the suite detected [1mzero[22m. The harness now builds the [38;5;10m.so[0m itself into a separate target dir and asserts it's newer than the source — after which [1m23 of 23[22m mutations are caught.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mThe tcache seeding could be defeated.[22m glibc only pushes freed chunks into the tcache while the bin is below capacity (7); beyond that they go to the fastbin, so a naive [38;5;10mfree(hi); free(lo)[0m seed stops controlling anything. That's what made [38;5;10mvalid_arity_dispatch_len3[0m fail in the release profile only when run after other tests. Seeding now drains the bin first, and a test pre-loads it with 0–12 chunks to guard the invariant.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m## The library's core difficulty[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10mcompare_allocations[0m compares the addresses of two live [38;5;10mmalloc(4)[0m blocks, so its result — and that of every [38;5;10marityN[0m, which folds it in — is a function of allocator state, not of its arguments. glibc's LIFO tcache flips the ordering on every call. A naive C-vs-Rust interleaved comparison always reports [38;5;10m(12, 11)[0m — and reports exactly the same when the [1mC library is compared against a second copy of itself[22m, which is the control test I added. So the suite forces the heap ordering before every measured call and runs each heap-sensitive row under [3mboth[23m orderings, making the [38;5;10mresult = 1[0m and [38;5;10mresult = 2[0m branches reachable on purpose. What stays environment-dependent (which ordering a fresh process starts in, since [38;5;10mdlopen[0m of a 4 MB Rust [38;5;10m.so[0m perturbs the heap differently than a 16 KB C one) is documented rather than papered over; a fixed answer in Rust would [3mdiverge[23m whenever C returned the other one. Identical [38;5;10mmalloc[0m/[38;5;10mfree[0m patterns are verified separately, in separate processes and via a minimal external C driver.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m## Behaviors that had to be preserved[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10marity[0m's parameter is [38;5;10munsigned char[0m in the definition but [38;5;10mint[0m in the header, and the compiled code compares only the low byte with an unsigned branch — so [38;5;10marity(256) == -1[0m and [38;5;10marity(-1)[0m is [3mnot[23m rejected. [38;5;10mparam1 % 4[0m goes negative for negative [38;5;10mparam1[0m, silently skipping the bitmask. Division truncates toward zero. Signed overflow wraps. [38;5;10muninit_ptr[0m aliases [38;5;10mptr1[0m, so the bonus keys off [38;5;10mval1[0m. All confirmed against the C at [38;5;10m-O0[0m through [38;5;10m-Os[0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
